---
/**
 * THE PAIRED WARD BENCH, INSIDE THE CONSOLE. The controller owns scenario state,
 * calculations, and canvas drawing; Astro owns landmarks and durable copy.
 *
 * THE RAIL REPLACED THE HEADER. There used to be a brand link, an Explore/Compare
 * pair and a brief link across the top of this page. All three are gone: the rail
 * is the console's only navigation, it carries the one brand mark, and the brief
 * link moved into the Analysis pane beside the method copy it belongs with.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * NO SCOPE SWITCHER ON THIS ROUTE, AND THE A/B PICKERS ARE WHY.
 *
 * shell/ScopeSwitcher.astro names ONE area. Compare holds TWO and neither is "the"
 * scope — the same reasoning this file already applied to the old Explore link,
 * which was static precisely because picking pane A's area would have been a guess
 * dressed as a destination. Rendering the switcher here would have had to pass
 * something, and the only value available at build time is the default pair: it
 * would have read "Ballygunge" to a visitor comparing Barrackpore against
 * Baruipur. A control stating a false scope is worse than no control.
 *
 * It could not have worked either. This shell is PRERENDERED and the pair arrives
 * as `?a=`/`?b=`, parsed client-side; and console-shell.ts only wires
 * `select[data-scope]` on a page with a `.stage` declaring one `data-area`, which
 * this is not. So the switcher would have been inert as well as untrue.
 *
 * The A/B selects ARE this route's scope control, so they sit where the switcher
 * sits on Explore — at the top of the sidebar, in the pane the rail opens. They
 * are populated at runtime by paired-controller.ts from `areaKeysInCity`, so
 * unlike a prerendered switcher they can tell the truth about the pair on screen.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * FOUR PANES, THREE OF WHICH SAY WHY THEY ARE EMPTY HERE.
 *
 * The rail's Layers, Reports and Scenarios navigate nowhere — they swap the
 * sidebar body. Rendering the rail with no bodies for them would have shipped
 * three buttons that do nothing on the one control every visitor has to use,
 * which is the defect this project has deleted repeatedly. So each one is here,
 * and each states in terms of what Compare IS why it holds nothing, with a way
 * out to the route where it does. That is the pattern HeatMapStage.astro already
 * uses twice, for an area with no artefacts and for the unbuilt scenario store.
 */
import IconRail from '../shell/IconRail.astro';
import PanelToggle from '../shell/PanelToggle.astro';
import { DEFAULT_AREA_PATH } from '../../../scripts/climate-engine/scope/paths.ts';
---
<main id="main" class="heat-compare" data-compare-root data-console data-renderer="canvas" aria-busy="true">
  {/* `route="analysis"` because this page IS Compare, and `pane="analysis"` because
      the pane below it is the one the server renders open. The rail derives the
      rest: Map becomes a plain link to Explore and loses its aria-pressed, since
      the toolbox it names is not in this document. */}
  <div class="rail-slot"><IconRail route="analysis" pane="analysis" /></div>

  <div class="heat-compare__console">
    <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Comparison console">
      {/* THE PANEL'S CHEVRON, AND IT IS ITS OWN ROW HERE RATHER THAN A HEADING'S.
          Explore slots this into the scope switcher's "Location" line; this route
          has no such line — the sidebar opens straight into a pane whose own
          heading belongs to the pane and changes with it — so the panel's top-right
          corner is a row of its own. Same component, same state, same paint. */}
      <div class="panel-head"><PanelToggle /></div>

      <div class="panes">
        {/* THE SCOPE CONTROL FOR THIS ROUTE, in the place Explore keeps its scope
            switcher. The selects are empty here on purpose: paired-controller.ts
            fills both from `areaKeysInCity` on every render, which is what keeps
            the pair inside one city and what makes them true about the ?a= the
            visitor actually arrived with. */}
        <div class="pane is-on" data-pane="analysis">
          <section class="pane-body" aria-labelledby="pane-analysis-h">
            <p class="pane-h" id="pane-analysis-h">Analysis</p>
            <p class="pane-note">One intervention package, two equal 1.4 km study windows, one pinned forcing record. Results show each ward’s response from its own baseline. They are not a ward ranking.</p>
            <label class="heat-compare__select-label">Ward A
              <select data-input="ward-a" aria-label="Ward A"></select>
            </label>
            <label class="heat-compare__select-label">Ward B
              <select data-input="ward-b" aria-label="Ward B"></select>
            </label>
            <button type="button" class="heat-compare__button heat-compare__button--quiet heat-compare__swap" data-action="swap">Swap wards <span aria-hidden="true">↔</span></button>
            <p class="pane-note">Both sides come from one city. A pair drawn across two of them would compare two climates and two currencies, and would price the result in neither.</p>
            <a class="pane-out" data-role="brief-link" href="/heat-map/brief/">Open brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="pane" data-pane="layers">
          <section class="pane-body" aria-labelledby="pane-layers-h">
            <p class="pane-h" id="pane-layers-h">Layers</p>
            <p class="pane-note">Layers turn on what the map draws. Compare draws no map: it renders two fixed 1.4 km thermal fields to a canvas from a single model run, so that the one thing differing between them is the fabric underneath.</p>
            <p class="pane-note">There is no basemap here to switch roads, canopy, footprints or ground-truth photography over — the tree needs a map, and the map takes one ward at a time.</p>
            <a class="pane-out" href={DEFAULT_AREA_PATH}>Open the map <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="pane" data-pane="reports">
          <section class="pane-body" aria-labelledby="pane-reports-h">
            <p class="pane-h" id="pane-reports-h">Reports</p>
            <p class="pane-note">The ward record is a document about ONE area: what was measured there, the out-of-sample error and sample size, and every source dataset with its licence. Compare holds two, and is a record of neither — the pairing is made in your browser and kept nowhere.</p>
            <p class="pane-note">What this route can hand you is the brief, under Analysis. It carries this pair and this package; it does not carry a ward’s measurements.</p>
            <a class="pane-out" href={DEFAULT_AREA_PATH}>Download a ward record from the map <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="pane" data-pane="scenarios">
          <section class="pane-body" aria-labelledby="pane-scenarios-h">
            <p class="pane-h" id="pane-scenarios-h">Scenarios</p>
            <p class="pane-note">Not built yet, and this route feels the gap twice. Compare runs exactly one package across both wards and keeps none of them: there is nowhere to save an intervention set, name it, or put two saved sets side by side — which here would be a comparison of comparisons.</p>
            <p class="pane-note">The sliders that build one are on the bench itself, under the shared package. The same three are on the map, one ward at a time.</p>
            <a class="pane-out" href={DEFAULT_AREA_PATH}>Open the map <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="heat-compare__main">
  <section class="heat-compare__intro" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
    <div>
      <p class="heat-compare__eyebrow">Urban Heat Explorer / Controlled comparison</p>
      {/* THE H1 STAYS ON THE PAGE. It is the document's title; the method paragraph
          that sat beside it has moved into the Analysis pane, where a reader
          looking for scope and limits will already be. */}
      <h1 id="compare-title">Same policy.<br /><em>Different fabric.</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <noscript>
    <p class="heat-compare__noscript">Compare results need JavaScript to run the model. The method, scope, and limits remain available in the <a href="/heat-map/brief/">research brief</a>.</p>
  </noscript>

  <div class="heat-compare__layout">
    <aside class="heat-compare__controls" data-sheet="collapsed" aria-label="Comparison workspace">
      <button class="heat-compare__sheet-handle" type="button" data-action="sheet-toggle" aria-expanded="false">
        <span class="heat-compare__handle-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span><b>Comparison workspace</b><small data-role="mobile-summary">Illustrative package</small></span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">⌃</span>
      </button>

      <div class="heat-compare__sheet-content">
        <div class="heat-compare__mobile-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Comparison workspace sections">
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="settings">Settings</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="evidence">Evidence</button>
        </div>

        <section class="heat-compare__control-panel" data-panel="settings" role="tabpanel">
          <div class="heat-compare__panel-heading">
            <p>Shared package</p>
            <span>Illustrative, editable</span>
          </div>
          <div class="heat-compare__control-stack">
            <label class="heat-compare__range">
              <span>Tree corridors <output data-output="trees">55%</output></span>
              <input data-input="trees" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="55" />
              <small>Modelled corridor-cell coverage</small>
            </label>
            <label class="heat-compare__range">
              <span>Cool roofs <output data-output="roofs">65%</output></span>
              <input data-input="roofs" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="65" />
              <small>Mapped roof-stock coverage</small>
            </label>
            <label class="heat-compare__range">
              <span>Green façades <output data-output="facades">35.0%</output></span>
              <input data-input="facades" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="0.1" value="35" />
              <small>Modelled programme intensity</small>
            </label>
          </div>
          <fieldset class="heat-compare__phase">
            <legend>Diurnal phase</legend>
            <label><input data-input="phase" type="radio" name="compare-phase" value="peak" checked /> <span>13:00 peak</span></label>
            <label><input data-input="phase" type="radio" name="compare-phase" value="retained" /> <span>22:00 retained</span></label>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="heat-compare__actions">
            <button type="button" class="heat-compare__button heat-compare__button--quiet" data-action="reset">Reset</button>
            <button type="button" class="heat-compare__button heat-compare__button--quiet" data-action="undo" disabled>Undo</button>
            <button type="button" class="heat-compare__button heat-compare__button--accent" data-action="share">Share state</button>
          </div>
          <label class="heat-compare__share-field" data-role="share-field" hidden>
            <span>Shareable URL</span>
            <input data-role="share-url" type="text" readonly />
          </label>
        </section>

        <section class="heat-compare__control-panel" data-panel="evidence" role="tabpanel" hidden>
          <div class="heat-compare__panel-heading"><p>Integrity stamp</p><span>Screening grade</span></div>
          <dl class="heat-compare__compact-evidence">
            <div><dt>Forcing</dt><dd data-role="forcing-label">Loading record</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd>192 × 192, canonical</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Backend</dt><dd data-role="backend-label">Selecting execution host</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>26–48°C, fixed</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="heat-compare__caveat">This interim reference is explicitly labelled until a sourced regional heat-day record is supplied. It is not live ward weather.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <section class="heat-compare__workbench" aria-label="Paired modelled surface-temperature maps">
      <div class="heat-compare__stagebar">
        <div class="heat-compare__status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-role="status">Preparing the paired model.</div>
        <button type="button" class="heat-compare__retry" data-action="retry" hidden>Retry model</button>
        <div class="heat-compare__view-controls" aria-label="Linked map view">
          <span class="heat-compare__renderer-state"><i aria-hidden="true"></i><b data-role="renderer-label">Canvas relief</b></span>
          <button type="button" data-view-mode="relief" aria-pressed="true">Relief</button>
          <button type="button" data-view-mode="top" aria-pressed="false">Top</button>
          <button type="button" data-action="motion" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Motion</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="heat-compare__sr-only" id="compare-3d-help">The optional animated view uses linked cameras. Drag horizontally to orbit both wards, use the mouse wheel to zoom, arrow keys to rotate, plus and minus to zoom, and zero to reset. All evidence is also available as text.</p>
      <div class="heat-compare__maps">
        <figure class="heat-compare__map-card" data-map-card="a">
          <div class="heat-compare__map-heading"><span class="heat-compare__map-index">A</span><div><h2 data-value="a-name">Ward A</h2><p data-value="a-descriptor">Loading study area</p></div><strong data-value="a-cooling">—</strong></div>
          <div class="heat-compare__map-surface">
            <canvas data-map-field="a" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            <canvas class="heat-compare__three" data-map-three="a" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" aria-describedby="compare-3d-help"></canvas>
            <output class="heat-compare__probe" data-map-probe="a" hidden></output>
            <div class="heat-compare__map-tools"><span data-role="map-mode-label">Canvas relief · adaptive fallback</span><button type="button" data-action="map-reset" data-map-reset="a">Reset linked</button></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption><span>1.4 km × 1.4 km</span><span>Thermal relief illustrative</span><span>26–48°C fixed scale</span></figcaption>
          <p class="heat-compare__pattern" data-value="a-pattern">Preparing spatial summary.</p>
        </figure>
        <figure class="heat-compare__map-card" data-map-card="b">
          <div class="heat-compare__map-heading"><span class="heat-compare__map-index">B</span><div><h2 data-value="b-name">Ward B</h2><p data-value="b-descriptor">Loading study area</p></div><strong data-value="b-cooling">—</strong></div>
          <div class="heat-compare__map-surface">
            <canvas data-map-field="b" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
            <canvas class="heat-compare__three" data-map-three="b" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true" aria-describedby="compare-3d-help"></canvas>
            <output class="heat-compare__probe" data-map-probe="b" hidden></output>
            <div class="heat-compare__map-tools"><span data-role="map-mode-label">Canvas relief · adaptive fallback</span><button type="button" data-action="map-reset" data-map-reset="b">Reset linked</button></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption><span>1.4 km × 1.4 km</span><span>Thermal relief illustrative</span><span>26–48°C fixed scale</span></figcaption>
          <p class="heat-compare__pattern" data-value="b-pattern">Preparing spatial summary.</p>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="heat-compare__map-legend" aria-label="Surface temperature scale"><span>26°C</span><i></i><span>48°C</span><b>Modelled surface temperature</b></div>
    </section>

    <aside class="heat-compare__evidence" aria-label="Comparison evidence">
      <div class="heat-compare__evidence-heading"><p>Comparison evidence</p><span>Atomic result</span></div>
      <div class="heat-compare__evidence-table" role="table" aria-label="Paired evidence metrics">
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row heat-compare__evidence-row--header"><span role="columnheader">Measure</span><span role="columnheader" data-value="a-name">A</span><span role="columnheader" data-value="b-name">B</span></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell">Baseline mean</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-baseline">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-baseline">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell">Scenario mean</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-scenario">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-scenario">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row heat-compare__evidence-row--accent"><span role="cell">Cooling from baseline</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-cooling">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-cooling">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell">Grid area &gt;40°C</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-hot-area">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-hot-area">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell">Hot-area change</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-hot-change">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-hot-change">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell" title="Modelled ward mean minus a fully vegetated reference cell under identical forcing. This is not a measured urban–rural heat-island value.">Δ vs all-green ref</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-green-reference">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-green-reference">—</strong></div>
        <div role="row" class="heat-compare__evidence-row"><span role="cell">Indicative capital</span><strong role="cell" data-value="a-cost">—</strong><strong role="cell" data-value="b-cost">—</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="heat-compare__delivery">
        <p>Delivered quantities</p>
        <div><span data-value="a-delivered">—</span><span data-value="b-delivered">—</span></div>
      </div>
      <dl class="heat-compare__integrity">
        <div><dt>Forcing</dt><dd data-role="forcing-label">Loading record</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Model</dt><dd>heat-model-v1</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd>hm-grid-192-v1</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Data</dt><dd>ward-geometry-v1</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Metrics</dt><dd>heat-metrics-v2</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Backend</dt><dd data-role="backend-label">Selecting execution host</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="heat-compare__caveat">Screening-grade output. It does not assess vulnerability, equity, feasibility, ownership, operations, maintenance, or investment priority.</p>
    </aside>
      </div><!-- /.heat-compare__layout -->
    </div><!-- /.heat-compare__main -->
  </div><!-- /.heat-compare__console -->
</main>

<style>
  .heat-compare{--ink:oklch(96% .008 210);--muted:oklch(68% .025 210);--faint:oklch(63% .024 210);--paper:oklch(12% .018 205);--surface:oklch(16% .024 205);--surface2:oklch(20% .03 205);--line:oklch(76% .055 205 / .2);--cyan:oklch(78% .105 202);--bronze:oklch(69% .08 75);--red:oklch(64% .16 28);--green:oklch(75% .09 145);min-height:100vh;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font-family:'Mona Sans',system-ui,sans-serif;padding:1.25rem clamp(1rem,4vw,4rem) 3.5rem;
    /* THE RAIL IS FIXED AND OUT OF FLOW, so the page reserves its column here.
       --rail IS NOT DECLARED ANYWHERE ON THIS ROUTE, and that is the fix rather
       than an omission. It used to be a literal here and a fallback inside
       shell/IconRail.astro, two numbers for one column with a test comparing
       them — which was tolerable only while the width was a constant. The rail
       expands and collapses now, so a per-route literal would have had to be TWO
       numbers per route, in three files, agreeing at both states.
       The rail declares both widths and the current one on :root instead, so this
       padding, the mobile sheet's offset below and the rail's own inline-size all
       read the one property the rail itself is sized by. There is no second copy
       left to drift, which is why the width guard in tests/unit/obos-shell.test.mjs
       now proves the absence rather than comparing two literals.
       --sidebar is the console column beside it. */
    --sidebar:300px;
    /* The console's panel ground, declared here for the same reason --rail-ground
       is declared in the rail bridge: HeatMapStage.astro's palette never loads on
       this route, so a token used here must be named here. The VALUE is the one
       the stage declares — one colour, two declarations. The duplicate-hex census
       is per-file and CANNOT see a drift between the two, which it was wrongly
       credited with here; `the console's two grounds are the same colour on both
       routes` in tests/unit/obos-shell.test.mjs is the guard that actually reads
       both files. */
    --panel-ground:var(--rail-ground);
    padding-inline-start:calc(var(--rail-edge) + clamp(1rem,4vw,4rem));}
  .heat-compare *{box-sizing:border-box}.heat-compare a{color:inherit}
  /* ── THE CONSOLE AROUND THE BENCH ───────────────────────────────────────────
     The rail is FIXED and full-height; the sidebar is a STICKY column beside a
     document that scrolls. That is the one structural difference from the Explore
     stage, which is `position:fixed;inset:0` over `body{overflow:hidden}` — this
     route is a scrolling document (`nativeScroll`), and a full-height grid would
     have cut the bench off at the viewport. */

  .rail-slot{
    position:fixed;inset-block:0;inset-inline-start:0;z-index:40;display:flex;
    /* THE TOKEN BRIDGE, AND IT IS A REMAP RATHER THAN A SECOND PALETTE.
       shell/IconRail.astro paints with the console's tokens, which are declared on
       .stage in HeatMapStage.astro — a stylesheet this route never loads. Two of
       the names it needs exist here with the OPPOSITE role: the stage's --paper is
       its brightest ink, and this file's --paper is the page's near-black ground.
       Left alone, the rail's aria-current rule painted the active button near-black
       on a rail whose background had silently unset — --rail-ground did not resolve,
       and an undefined custom property makes the whole declaration invalid rather
       than falling back. Nothing errored; the rail was simply not there.
       So the three are declared HERE, on the rail's own wrapper and nowhere else.
       --paper POINTS AT this file's --ink rather than restating its value, so the
       colour has one spelling and the bench's own rules keep the --paper they were
       written against. */
    --rail-ground:#091416f5;
    --paper:var(--ink);
    --mono:'Noplato Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;
  }

  .heat-compare__console{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem;align-items:start}
  .heat-compare__main{min-inline-size:0}

  /* `is-collapsed` is console-shell.ts's, set when the open pane's rail button is
     clicked again. `auto` in the grid above is what lets the column go to zero
     when it lands, rather than leaving a 300px hole. */
  .sidebar{inline-size:var(--sidebar);position:sticky;top:1.25rem;
    max-block-size:calc(100dvh - 2.5rem);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-block-size:0;
    /* THE SAME PANEL GROUND THE STAGE USES, written here because this route never
       loads HeatMapStage.astro — the same reason the rail's token bridge above
       exists. A hex rather than a var() would be the duplicate-colour defect the
       census catches; declared once in the bridge, both sidebars read one value. */
    background:var(--panel-ground);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:.85rem;overflow:hidden}
  .sidebar.is-collapsed{display:none}
  /* THE SAME FACT, READ BEFORE THE SIDEBAR EXISTS. shell/layout-state.ts's
     pre-paint script runs where the rail is, at the top of the console, and the
     parser has not reached this element yet — so the preference lands on <html>
     and this rule carries it down. console-shell.ts's `paint` writes BOTH this
     attribute and the class above, in one function, so they cannot disagree; the
     class is the element's own state and this is the document-level mirror that
     exists only to be applied early. Without it the sidebar renders open on every
     load and then vanishes once the module script mounts. */
  html[data-panel="collapsed"] .sidebar{display:none}
  .panel-head{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;padding:8px 8px 0;flex:none}

  /* One grid cell, every pane stacked in it, so the cross-fade has nothing to
     reflow. `visibility` rather than `display:none` keeps a hidden pane out of the
     tab order and the accessibility tree while still letting opacity animate. */
  .panes{flex:1;min-block-size:0;display:grid}
  .pane{grid-area:1/1;min-block-size:0;overflow:auto;
    opacity:0;transform:translateY(6px);visibility:hidden;pointer-events:none;
    transition:opacity .22s ease,transform .22s ease,visibility 0s .22s}
  .pane.is-on{opacity:1;transform:none;visibility:visible;pointer-events:auto;
    transition:opacity .22s ease,transform .22s ease,visibility 0s}

  .pane-body{padding:1rem;display:grid;gap:.75rem;align-content:start}
  .pane-body>*{margin:0}
  .pane-h{font-family:'Noplato Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.14em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--faint)}
  .pane-note{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)}
  /* The two bench controls that moved into the Analysis pane bring their own
     spacing from a stacked panel; the grid gap here already provides it. */
  .pane-body .heat-compare__select-label{margin-bottom:0}
  .pane-body .heat-compare__swap{margin-top:0}
  /* THE WAY OUT of a pane that is empty on this route. Without one, a reader who
     opened Layers to find no layers is told why and left there. */
  .pane-out{font-family:'Noplato Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:.6rem;letter-spacing:.08em;
    text-transform:uppercase;text-decoration:none;color:var(--cyan);justify-self:start;
    border-bottom:1px solid transparent;padding-bottom:2px;transition:border-color .18s}
  .pane-out:hover{border-bottom-color:var(--cyan)}
  .pane-out:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--cyan);outline-offset:3px}

